# 必考词 Unit18
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit18核心词汇

{{precedent}}{{/ˈpresɪdənt}}{{n. 先例； precedent}}{{The ruling set a legal precedent.}}
{{precise}}{{/prɪˈsaɪs}}{{adj. 精确的； precise}}{{Can you give me a more precise estimate?}}
{{predict}}{{/prɪˈdɪkt}}{{v. 预测； predict}}{{It is difficult to predict the outcome of the election.}}
{{predominant}}{{/prɪˈdɒmɪnənt}}{{adj. 主要的； predominant；占主导地位的}}{{English is the predominant language in this region.}}
{{prejudice}}{{/ˈpredʒudɪs}}{{n./v. 偏见； prejudice；损害}}{{Racial prejudice remains a serious problem in society.}}
{{preliminary}}{{/prɪˈlɪmɪnəri}}{{adj./n. 初步的； preliminary；准备工作}}{{The preliminary results are very promising.}}
{{premise}}{{/ˈpremɪs}}{{n. 前提； premise； premises（房产）}}{{The argument is based on a false premise.}}
{{premium}}{{/ˈpriːmiəm}}{{n./adj. 保险费； premium；优质的}}{{Customers are willing to pay a premium for quality products.}}
{{prescribe}}{{/prɪˈskraɪb}}{{v. 开处方； prescribe；规定}}{{The doctor prescribed a new medication for her.}}
{{preserve}}{{/prɪˈzɜːv}}{{v. 保存； preserve；保护}}{{We must preserve our cultural heritage.}}
{{preside}}{{/prɪˈzaɪd}}{{v. 主持； preside}}{{The judge presided over the trial.}}
{{prestige}}{{/preˈstiːʒ}}{{n. 威望； prestige}}{{The university has great prestige worldwide.}}
{{presume}}{{/prɪˈzjuːm}}{{v. 假定； presume；冒昧}}{{I presume you have read the report.}}
{{prevail}}{{/prɪˈveɪl}}{{v. 盛行； prevail；获胜}}{{Common sense prevailed in the end.}}
{{prevent}}{{/prɪˈvent}}{{v. 阻止； prevent}}{{The vaccine can prevent the disease.}}
{{previous}}{{/ˈpriːviəs}}{{adj. 先前的； previous}}{{She had no previous experience in management.}}
{{primary}}{{/ˈpraɪməri}}{{adj. 主要的； primary；初级的}}{{Education is the primary concern for parents.}}
{{prime}}{{/praɪm}}{{adj./n. 主要的； prime；全盛期}}{{He is in the prime of his career.}}
{{principal}}{{/ˈprɪnsəpl}}{{adj./n. 主要的； principal；校长}}{{The principal spoke at the graduation ceremony.}}
{{principle}}{{/ˈprɪnsəpl}}{{n. 原则； principle；原理}}{{He is a man of strong principles.}}
{{prior}}{{/ˈpraɪər}}{{adj. 在先的； prior；更重要的}}{{Prior to the meeting, please read the report.}}
{{priority}}{{/praɪˈɒrəti}}{{n. 优先事项； priority}}{{Safety is our top priority.}}
{{privilege}}{{/ˈprɪvəlɪdʒ}}{{n. 特权； privilege}}{{Education is a right, not a privilege.}}
{{probe}}{{/prəʊb}}{{v./n. 探索； probe；调查}}{{The committee launched a probe into the corruption allegations.}}
{{proceed}}{{/prəˈsiːd}}{{v. 继续进行； proceed}}{{Please proceed with the next item on the agenda.}}
{{proclaim}}{{/prəˈkleɪm}}{{v. 宣布； proclaim；表明}}{{The president proclaimed a state of emergency.}}
{{productive}}{{/prəˈdʌktɪv}}{{adj. 高效的； productive；多产的}}{{It was a very productive meeting.}}
{{profession}}{{/prəˈfeʃn}}{{n. 职业； profession}}{{She chose teaching as her profession.}}
{{profit}}{{/ˈprɒfɪt}}{{n./v. 利润； profit；获利}}{{The company made a significant profit last year.}}
{{profound}}{{/prəˈfaʊnd}}{{adj. 深刻的； profound；渊博的}}{{The book had a profound impact on my thinking.}}
{{prohibit}}{{/prəˈhɪbɪt}}{{v. 禁止； prohibit}}{{Smoking is prohibited in public places.}}
{{project}}{{/prəˈdʒekt}}{{v. 预测； project；投射}}{{The company projects a 20% growth in revenue.}}
{{prominent}}{{/ˈprɒmɪnənt}}{{adj. 突出的； prominent；著名的}}{{He is a prominent figure in the field of science.}}
{{promote}}{{/prəˈməʊt}}{{v. 促进； promote；晋升}}{{The campaign promotes healthy eating habits.}}
{{prompt}}{{/prɒmpt}}{{adj./v. 迅速的； prompt；促使}}{{The incident prompted a review of safety procedures.}}
{{prone}}{{/prəʊn}}{{adj. 易于的； prone；俯卧的}}{{Children are prone to ear infections.}}
{{propaganda}}{{/ˌprɒpəˈɡændə}}{{n. 宣传； propaganda}}{{The government used propaganda to influence public opinion.}}
{{propel}}{{/prəˈpel}}{{v. 推动； propel；驱使}}{{Technology has propelled the growth of the economy.}}
{{proper}}{{/ˈprɒpər}}{{adj. 适当的； proper；正确的}}{{You should wear proper clothing for the occasion.}}
{{property}}{{/ˈprɒpəti}}{{n. 财产； property；房地产}}{{The property market has been booming.}}
{{proportion}}{{/prəˈpɔːʃn}}{{n. 比例； proportion}}{{A large proportion of the budget is spent on healthcare.}}
{{proposal}}{{/prəˈpəʊzl}}{{n. 提议； proposal；求婚}}{{The committee approved the proposal unanimously.}}
{{propose}}{{/prəˈpəʊz}}{{v. 提议； propose；打算}}{{She proposed a new strategy for the company.}}
{{prosecute}}{{/ˈprɒsɪkjuːt}}{{v. 起诉； prosecute；检举}}{{The company was prosecuted for violating environmental laws.}}
{{prospect}}{{/ˈprɒspekt}}{{n. 前景； prospect；可能性}}{{The prospects for economic recovery look good.}}
{{prosper}}{{/ˈprɒspər}}{{v. 繁荣； prosper；兴旺}}{{The business has prospered under new management.}}
{{protocol}}{{/ˈprəʊtəkɒl}}{{n. 协议； protocol；礼仪}}{{All staff must follow the safety protocol.}}
{{province}}{{/ˈprɒvɪns}}{{n. 省份； province；领域}}{{She comes from a coastal province.}}
{{provision}}{{/prəˈvɪʒn}}{{n. 提供； provision；条款}}{{The provision of clean water is essential.}}
{{provoke}}{{/prəˈvəʊk}}{{v. 激怒； provoke；引起}}{{His remarks provoked an angry response.}}
{{prudent}}{{/ˈpruːdnt}}{{adj. 谨慎的； prudent}}{{It would be prudent to save some money for emergencies.}}
{{pursue}}{{/pəˈsjuː}}{{v. 追求； pursue；从事}}{{She decided to pursue a career in medicine.}}
{{qualify}}{{/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪ}}{{v. 使合格； qualify；限制}}{{He qualified as a doctor last year.}}
{{quote}}{{/kwəʊt}}{{v./n. 引用； quote；报价}}{{She quoted a famous line from Shakespeare.}}
{{radical}}{{/ˈrædɪkl}}{{adj./n. 激进的； radical；根本的}}{{The government proposed radical reforms to the education system.}}
{{random}}{{/ˈrændəm}}{{adj. 随机的； random}}{{The numbers were selected at random.}}
{{range}}{{/reɪndʒ}}{{n./v. 范围； range；变化}}{{The hotel offers a wide range of services.}}
{{rank}}{{/ræŋk}}{{n./v. 等级； rank；排名}}{{The university ranks among the top ten in the country.}}
{{rational}}{{/ˈræʃənl}}{{adj. 理性的； rational}}{{We need to make a rational decision based on the facts.}}
{{raw}}{{/rɔː}}{{adj. 生的； raw；未加工的}}{{The data is still in its raw form.}}
{{react}}{{/riˈækt}}{{v. 反应； react}}{{How did the audience react to the performance?}}
{{realm}}{{/relm}}{{n. 领域； realm；王国}}{{He made significant contributions to the realm of science.}}
{{reasonable}}{{/ˈriːznəbl}}{{adj. 合理的； reasonable}}{{The prices are very reasonable.}}
{{rebel}}{{/rɪˈbel}}{{v./n. 反叛； rebel；叛乱者}}{{The soldiers rebelled against their commander.}}
{{recall}}{{/rɪˈkɔːl}}{{v. 回忆； recall；召回}}{{I can't recall his name.}}
{{receipt}}{{/rɪˈsiːt}}{{n. 收据； receipt；收到}}{{Please keep the receipt for your records.}}
{{recession}}{{/rɪˈseʃn}}{{n. 衰退； recession；萧条}}{{The economy went into a deep recession.}}
{{reckon}}{{/ˈrekən}}{{v. 认为； reckon；估计}}{{I reckon he's about forty years old.}}
{{recognize}}{{/ˈrekəɡnaɪz}}{{v. 认出； recognize；承认}}{{I didn't recognize him at first.}}
{{recommend}}{{/ˌrekəˈmend}}{{v. 推荐； recommend；建议}}{{I recommend this book to anyone interested in history.}}
{{reconcile}}{{/ˈrekənsaɪl}}{{v. 调和； reconcile；和解}}{{They reconciled their differences after the argument.}}
{{recover}}{{/rɪˈkʌvər}}{{v. 恢复； recover；收回}}{{The economy recovered quickly after the crisis.}}
{{recruit}}{{/rɪˈkruːt}}{{v./n. 招募； recruit；新成员}}{{The company is recruiting new staff.}}
{{reduce}}{{/rɪˈdjuːs}}{{v. 减少； reduce；降低}}{{We need to reduce our energy consumption.}}
{{refer}}{{/rɪˈfɜːr}}{{v. 提到； refer；参考}}{{Please refer to the handbook for more details.}}
{{reflect}}{{/rɪˈflekt}}{{v. 反映； reflect；思考}}{{The report reflects the current state of the economy.}}
{{reform}}{{/rɪˈfɔːm}}{{v./n. 改革； reform}}{{The government introduced education reforms.}}
{{refuge}}{{/ˈrefjuːdʒ}}{{n. 避难所； refuge；庇护}}{{The camp provided refuge for displaced families.}}
{{regime}}{{/reɪˈʒiːm}}{{n. 政权； regime；制度}}{{The regime was overthrown in a revolution.}}
{{register}}{{/ˈredʒɪstər}}{{v./n. 登记； register；注册}}{{You need to register for the course in advance.}}
{{regulate}}{{/ˈreɡjuleɪt}}{{v. 调节； regulate；管理}}{{The government regulates the banking industry.}}
{{reinforce}}{{/ˌriːɪnˈfɔːs}}{{v. 加强； reinforce；增援}}{{The evidence reinforces his argument.}}
{{reject}}{{/rɪˈdʒekt}}{{v. 拒绝； reject；驳回}}{{The proposal was rejected by the committee.}}
{{relate}}{{/rɪˈleɪt}}{{v. 与…有关； relate；叙述}}{{The article relates to the current political situation.}}
{{release}}{{/rɪˈliːs}}{{v./n. 释放； release；发布}}{{The company released a new version of the software.}}
{{relevant}}{{/ˈreləvənt}}{{adj. 相关的； relevant}}{{Please provide relevant information for the report.}}
{{relieve}}{{/rɪˈliːv}}{{v. 缓解； relieve；解除}}{{The medicine helped relieve the pain.}}
{{reluctant}}{{/rɪˈlʌktənt}}{{adj. 不情愿的； reluctant}}{{She was reluctant to accept the offer.}}
{{rely}}{{/rɪˈlaɪ}}{{v. 依赖； rely；信赖}}{{You can rely on me for support.}}
{{remain}}{{/rɪˈmeɪn}}{{v. 保持； remain；剩余}}{{The situation remains unchanged.}}
{{remark}}{{/rɪˈmɑːk}}{{v./n. 评论； remark；注意到}}{{He made a remark about the weather.}}
{{remedy}}{{/ˈremədi}}{{n./v. 补救措施； remedy；治疗}}{{There is no easy remedy for this problem.}}
{{remote}}{{/rɪˈməʊt}}{{adj. 遥远的； remote；偏僻的}}{{The village is in a remote area of the country.}}
{{render}}{{/ˈrendər}}{{v. 使成为； render；提供}}{{The accident rendered him unconscious.}}
